Decisions reflected (see DECISIONS.md):
  AD-1   Grading mode is per assignment
  AD-2   The instructor's test suite is the autograder
  AD-3   Target identifiers are a checked contract
  AD-4   The autograder container holds the LLM API key
  AD-5   results.json is written before grading starts
  AD-6   Functional test outcomes are not stored
  AD-7   ai_needed defaults ON; the suite opts targets out
  AD-8   IMMEDIATE never defers to the nightly run
  AD-9   The token guard
  AD-10  Optional test context feeds the prompt
  AD-11  The container asks the service what to do

Reporting library surface, both calls optional:
  ai_not_needed(target)
  add_test_context(target, note)

The AI phase runs in EVERY autograder run and holds no policy. It asks
GET /submissions/{id}/action and gets GRADE, DEFER or REEMIT. The
nightly trigger sets submission.ai_authorized_at BEFORE clicking
rerun; that flag is how the service tells a submission run from a
triggered rerun.

submission_target: ai_needed, completed_at, last_error. No status enum
and no attempt counter. Retries live inside one run; failure is
terminal and reported in results.json in both modes.

